hello and welcome to the new review your  source for everything anime and manga  and more specifically welcome to hunt  hunter 101 the series that breaks down  everyone and everything in the hunt  hunter world and today we are going to  be examining the most prolific  organization within the entire series as  well as its namesake  being the hunter association the hunter  association is a global third party  organization designed to cultivate  world-class talent in almost every area  imaginable and focus it towards solving  various problems achieving certain goals  or in some cases even mobilizing  offensive and defensive operations  on behalf of very very wealthy clients  the association itself is located in  swadani city although it has never been  confirmed exactly where in the world  this is in fact i can't even give you so  much as a continent it's just another  one of those miscellaneous metropolises  but as such a hunter generally has the  choice to either take jobs issued to the  association by the aforementioned  wealthy clients or simply use their  status within the association to pursue  their own personal objectives  so for example if you were a hunter then  your personal objective would be to  subscribe to the new  review for regular hunt under content  uploaded straight into your youtube feed  which i think we both know would be  pretty damn awesome  but before we go too much further i  actually think it is important to  briefly dwell on the question of what  exactly is a hunter and i have made a  whole video regarding this so please do  feel free to watch that but despite  their prominence in the series this  profession is rarely explored primarily  because we see most of the series  through the eyes of gon and killua  neither of which particularly pursue the  profession of hunter despite being  licensed to do so i mean i guess you  could make the argument that they are  hunting jing but that is beside the  point hunter is actually quite a broad  and vague term in this world and it can  encompass effectively any top tier  profession that one can think of  so of course we have basic forms of  hunting such as treasure hunting or wild  game hunting the wild game in this world  sometimes being extraordinarily magical  beasts but what it means to be a hunter  is almost  entirely up to the individual in  question so to illustrate a classic  definition would be someone like bisky  who is a treasure hunter but expanding a  bit further we can also look at  mizeistom who is a crime hunter and that  basically means that he is a glorified  global detective but what a hunter is  can also delve into the abstract when we  encounter individuals like say cutie  beauty who is referred to as a cute  hunter and whose purpose is to solely  maintain the beauty of others  and this can be applied to quite  literally any profession so for example  if i were to  somehow pass the hunter exam then i  would probably label myself as a youtube  hunter which basically would mean that i  pursue this platform  only with all of the resources of the  hunter association available to me which  you know that would be nice and as such  there is an incredibly huge breadth of  different types of hunters so many so  that that's the reason why i made a  whole video on them but it is important  to understand that as far as the  association goes this  is essentially an organization of  world-class professionals who  in an ideal world come together to  mutually assist the goals of one another  although the large majority of hunters  do still operate alone  and as such it is actually entirely  possible and common for hunters to  become licensed and then just completely  ignore the actual association however  despite this grand freedom there are  still a collective of strict rules that  all hunters must obey  decreed by the association which are  known as the hunter bylaws and these  bylaws are a set of 10 rules almost a  form of 10 commandments and very much  acts as the glue that prevents the  association from descending into pure  anarchy and the first by-law is simply  that  hunters must always be on the hunt for  something which i imagine is implemented  to stop hunters from passing the exam  acquiring large amounts of wealth and  just retiring with no further impact on  the world although to be perfectly  honest i really don't see how this  particular bylaw would be strictly  enforced especially when the definition  of a hunter is just so  vague i mean even in my aforementioned  example of retirement i could just claim  to be a leisure hunter or something  constantly in pursuit of the greatest  pleasures that life has to offer with  minimal effort required and i really  don't see the association questioning  that  the next bylaw is a bit more restrictive  though being that hunters must have a  minimal understanding of martial arts  this includes learning nen which makes  sense because nen in the hunt hunter  world is a global standard of talent  even if an end user is unaware that they  are invoking it like komagi for example  next up once a hunter is licensed that  license cannot be revoked for any reason  and on the flip side a license will not  be reissued for any reason and the only  reason why i would come to question this  has to do with the next bylaw which is  that hunters shall not target other  hunters  unless they commit heinous crimes so  basically a hunter that commits crimes  won't have their licence revoked however  it will make them free game to any other  hunter  who so desired to track them down and i  imagine that a good example of someone  like this would be say ilmizoldic who is  a licensed hunter who has caused  incredible amounts of civilian  casualties during the chairman election  arc or actually an even better example  would be shalnok from the phantom troupe  who is both a hunter and has a class a  bounty and those really are the most  necessary rules to be aware of and the  next six pretty much just dive balls  deep into administration but we'll go  through them nonetheless because it does  greatly impact our understanding of the  association as a whole so next rule one  star  is given to a hunter who produces  remarkable achievements in a particular  field  two stars are given to a hunter who  fulfills the five articles which is  basically referring to the five previous  rules that we've explored holds an  official position  and has mentored a junior hunter who is  awarded a star three stars given to a  hunter who fulfills the six articles aka  the six prior rules we've explored and  produces remarkable achievements in  multiple fields the chief executive of  the hunter association must earn the  confidence of a majority of his  colleagues  when the position of chairman is vacated  the vote to elect the next chairman must  be conducted at once and deputy power is  given to the vice chairman in the  meantime the authority to decide on a  method to select new members is given to  the chairman however to significantly  change existing methods  requires the confidence of a majority of  colleagues which i suppose means holding  a referendum which all members of the  association can participate in  and finally any matter not mentioned  here will be decided in a cabinet  consisting of the chairman vice chairman  and staff advisors the chairman has the  authority to select vice chairman and  staff  and all right cool that's a lot like a  lot of rules there many of which are  only relevant to one particular arc in  the series but they are very important  as we now move on to examine the  hierarchy of the association  and at the very pinnacle we have the  chairman who for most of the series was  isaac netaro the chairman possesses  overwhelming power and influence within  the organization with no effective  checks or balances onset influence and  the direction in which they wish to take  the organization so obviously as you can  tell from that the decision to elect a  chairman is absolutely paramount because  if the wrong person were to be installed  then it could have incredible  ramifications on not just the  association but actually the entirety of  the human world and just on that i would  very much argue that much of the way we  see the hunt hunter world can be  attributed directly to chairman netro  whose leadership was highly focused on  fostering the strong whilst ignoring the  weak a trend that you can see almost  everywhere in the series but thus far  hunthunter has known three association  chairmans one of which was obviously  netaro who was the 12th chairman but  also paristan hill was the chairman for  all of like  two seconds and most currently we have  14th german cheetah yorkshire in charge  and within the association there is also  a vice chairman position an individual  who is granted almost as much control as  the chairman themselves however they  mainly exist to serve as backup in the  event that the chairman becomes  incapacitated or the position otherwise  deemed vacant in that case the vice  chairman serves as an interim however  they are not instantly promoted and an  election must take place within the  association  to decide who will permanently fill the  position however in regards to the vice  chairman no  election is necessary and that position  is filled entirely at the discretion of  the chairman and in the series paris and  hill would be the most famous vice  chairman although cheetah was also vice  chairman during pariston's two-second  chairmanship venture but very  interestingly it's currently unknown if  the association actually has a vice  chairman which is kind of odd to think  about because plenty of time has passed  and cheatle seems like a fairly strict  administrative law and order type but  there you go in addition to these roles  of leadership though there does also  exist an extended pool of staff advisors  who were assembled by the foreman  chairman netro and known as the zodiacs  this group comprises 12 individuals who  have had their skills recognized by the  chairman and are employed to act as  direct counselors as well as in the case  of netero  sparring partners with that said this  group is fairly disorganized due to  netro is an eclectic taste in  individuals and they don't function very  well as a cohesive unit having split  into various subfactions between them  however the zodiacs do contain some of  the most renowned and powerful hunters  in the world and now i would also be  quite remiss not to mention  beans a fascinating existence whose  humanity has neither been confirmed nor  denied however he does act as the  chairman's personal secretary and has  now i suppose technically served under  at least three different chairmen but  beans is probably the epitome of loyalty  within the hunter association and has  always  acted with the best interests of the  organization in mind something that i'm  not sure we can say about  literally any other character now  stepping further down into the  day-to-day running of the association  there have been  four widely identified branches of  operations that exist within this  extensive organization the most  prominent of which would be the exam  commission a task force entrusted with  the management of the annual hunter exam  and this includes structuring the format  of the exam as well as nominating  examiners both of which do change quite  radically from one year to the next the  examiners must  of course all be hunters and very  notably they are not paid for their role  as examiners although to be fair money  is really no object qualified hunters in  fact of the top 100 richest people in  the hunt hunter world  60 of them are hunters but in addition  to this there are also an incredible  suit of associates to the exam committee  many of whom are designated with the  role of pre-examiners who are charged  with weeding out those who are  completely unfit to even take the hunter  exam  and examples of individuals like this  would be the very vaguely named  captain or the quiz lady the one  constant with the exam committee though  is that the chairman of the association  also acts as the head of the exam  commission now next up we have the  review board which is a fairly  mysterious group actually who manage  assignments and delegate client requests  to hunters within the association  however what's really fascinating about  the review board is that they seem to  exist on a higher plane of power than  even that of the chairman as netra has  stated that even he was unable to deny  their decision once made so they seem to  represent an entirely new plane of power  altogether but rather sadly we are  currently unaware of even a single  character  who comprises a member of this board  moving on though from time to time a  temporary operation cohort is formed  known as the election task force which  is only really relevant when it comes  time to fill the chairman position which  doesn't happen often and of course its  purpose is to ensure the smooth running  of democracy within the association  as well as defining the structure of the  election itself and leadership of this  council in the series was actually given  to beans with the zodiac members also  acting as advisors and implementers and  finally we have the disciplinary  committee a group whose purpose has not  been solidly defined but one could make  the assumption that they exist to ensure  order within the association  although as i've said before exactly how  this is possible is kind of unknown  mainly due to the large degree of  freedom and immunity that hunters are  granted in general but we do have at  least one example of a member of the  disciplinary committee who would be a  man by the name of bushido ambitious  although rather unfortunately he was  probably murdered by hisoka during the  chairman election arc but apart from  that the only formal hierarchy that  still remains to be explored is the star  system which we briefly covered in the  hunter bylaws which does go on to state  their requirements however for  particularly accomplished hunters they  are awarded with a star rating from one  to three with three obviously being the  highest and in fact in the series we  currently only know of three characters  who have achieved this being cheadle  harriston and another zodiac member  being bought by gigante so in essence  this organization is still quite the  mysterious entity  despite the focus given to it in the  series during the latter arcs it still  raises a lot of questions in terms of  how the association is funded given that  they are a completely independent  organization like for example do various  countries of the world perhaps the v6  each pay into it in exchange for having  access to specialty hunters or is this a  completely privately funded endeavor who  knows maybe it even operates as a  phantom nation and it taxes its hunters  but i kind of doubt that in any case it  mainly forms a background feature of the  series anyway a rough framework to set  against the adventures of our main  protagonists although the association  itself is quite fascinating and i do  hope that we continue to learn more  about it in the future  but what do you guys think please do  leave your thoughts in the comments  below or even join my discord server and  if you're keen for some more hunt on  content then please do feel free to  check out some of my other videos or  even subscribe to the channel for  regular hunt on glory delivered straight  into your youtube feed but for now this  has been the new world review and i'll  see you next time

